* [[June 1]] 
** [[2025 Polish presidential election]]: [[Karol Nawrocki]] is narrowly elected [[President of Poland]] in the second round of voting, beating [[Rafał Trzaskowski]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-06-02 |title=Poland election: Conservative historian Nawrocki wins presidential vote |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx27897vedno |access-date=2025-06-02 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB |archive-date=May 23, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260523112323/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx27897vedno |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-06-02 |title=Conservative Karol Nawrocki wins Poland's presidential election |url=https://apnews.com/article/poland-presidential-election-karol-nawrocki-80a99eeb7a2f3ae64260a9263e7028ee |access-date=2025-06-02 |agency=Associated Press |language=en |archive-date=June 3, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250603063722/https://apnews.com/article/poland-presidential-election-karol-nawrocki-80a99eeb7a2f3ae64260a9263e7028ee |url-status=live }}</ref>
** [[Operation Spiderweb]]: Ukraine launches a large drone attack on Russian military bases. More than 40 aircraft of the [[Russian Air Force]] are attacked.<ref>{{cite web |title=Ukraine's audacious drone attack sends critical message to Russia - and the West |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c0r1jv0rn0ko |work=BBC News |access-date=2 June 2025 |date=1 June 2025}}</ref>
* [[June 3]]
** [[2025 South Korean presidential election]]: After being pushed forward as a result of the [[impeachment of Yoon Suk Yeol]], [[Lee Jae Myung]] wins the election, beating [[Kim Moon-soo (politician)|Kim Moon-soo]].<ref>{{cite news|first1=Jessie|last1=Yeung|first2=YoonJung|last2=Seo|first3=Gawon|last3=Bae|first4=Mike|last4=Valerio|first5=Lauren|last5=Kent|date=June 4, 2025|url=https://edition.cnn.com/2025/06/03/asia/south-korea-presidential-election-results-intl-hnk|title=South Korea's opposition leader Lee wins election as voters punish conservatives after martial law chaos|location=Seoul, South Korea|publisher=[[CNN]]|access-date=August 27, 2025}}</ref>
** [[2025 Mongolian protests]]: [[Luvsannamsrain Oyun-Erdene]] resigns as [[Prime Minister of Mongolia]] after losing a no-confidence vote in the [[State Great Khural]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-06-03 |title=Mongolia PM resigns amid protests over his son's lavish lifestyle |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5yg8dxv5w9o |access-date=2025-06-09 |publisher=BBC |language=en-GB |archive-date=June 4, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250604221550/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5yg8dxv5w9o |url-status=live }}</ref>
*[[June 10]] – 10 people are killed and more than 30 others injured after a gunman [[2025 Graz school shooting|opens fire]] at a school in [[Graz]], [[Austria]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Krupa |first=Jakub |date=2025-06-10 |title=10 people dead and 12 injured in school shooting in city of Graz in Austria – Europe live |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/jun/10/russia-strikes-drown-peace-efforts-zelenskyy-ukraine-europe-latest-news-updates |access-date=2025-06-10 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>
*[[June 12]] – [[Air India Flight 171]], a London-bound [[Boeing 787]], crashes into a building after take-off from [[Ahmedabad]], India, killing 229 passengers, 12 crew on board, and 19 people on the ground. [[List of aviation accidents and incidents with a sole survivor|One passenger survives the crash]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Khanna |first=Sumit |date=2025-06-24 |title=Authorities identify all but one of 260 victims of Air India plane crash |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/aerospace-defense/authorities-identify-all-one-260-victims-air-india-plane-crash-2025-06-24/ |access-date=2025-06-26 |work=Reuters |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-06-29 |title=Air India crash: DNA testing complete, final death toll stands at 260 |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/india/air-india-crash-dna-testing-complete-final-death-toll-stands-at-260/articleshow/122138572.cms?from=mdr |access-date=2025-06-30 |work=The Economic Times |issn=0013-0389}}</ref> It is the first fatal crash and [[hull loss]] involving a [[Boeing 787 Dreamliner]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=June 12, 2025 |title=London-bound Air India flight with more than 240 aboard crashes after takeoff from Ahmedabad, India |url=https://apnews.com/article/india-plane-crash-cad8dad5cd0e92795b03d357404af5f8 |access-date=June 12, 2025 |agency=[[Associated Press]] |archive-date=June 13, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250613204848/https://apnews.com/article/india-plane-crash-cad8dad5cd0e92795b03d357404af5f8 |url-status=live }}</ref>
*[[June 13]] – [[Twelve-Day War]]: Israel conducts air strikes against Iran's nuclear facilities, killing military commanders including [[Hossein Salami]]; Iran retaliates.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/c93ydeqyq71t |title=Israel targets Iran's nuclear sites, killing military commanders and scientists in major attack |date=13 June 2025 |website=BBC News |publisher=BBC |accessdate=13 June 2025 |archive-date=June 13, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250613002158/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/c93ydeqyq71t |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last1=Fassihi |first1=Farnaz |last2=Nauman |first2=Qasim |last3=Boxerman |first3=Aaron |last4=Kingsley |first4=Patrick |last5=Bergman |first5=Ronen |date=2025-06-13 |title=Israel Strikes Iran's Nuclear Program, Killing Top Military Officials: Live Updates |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2025/06/12/world/israel-iran-us-nuclear |access-date=2025-06-13 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331 |archive-date=June 18, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250618141401/https://www.nytimes.com/live/2025/06/12/world/israel-iran-us-nuclear |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[June 14]] – [[July 13]] – The [[2025 FIFA Club World Cup]] is held in the [[United States]], and [[2025 FIFA Club World Cup final|is won]] by [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]].<ref>{{cite web|last=Lowe|first=Sid|title=Chelsea stun PSG to win Club World Cup after Cole Palmer's cool double|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2025/jul/13/chelsea-stun-psg-to-win-club-world-cup-after-cole-palmers-cool-double|website=The Guardian|access-date=14 July 2025|date=13 July 2025}}</ref>
* [[June 14]] – The [[No Kings protests (June 2025)|No Kings protests]] occur across many cities in the U.S., as well as Canada, Europe, Japan and Mexico, against Donald Trump.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-06-14 |title=Mexico and Canada Unite with US, Japan, Germany, Colombia, Italy, Portugal, Spain and Many More Countries in Supporting No Kings Protest and it Becomes Global, How Travel Gets Impact This Weekend - Travel And Tour World |url=https://www.travelandtourworld.com/news/article/mexico-and-canada-unite-with-us-japan-germany-colombia-italy-portugal-spain-and-many-more-countries-in-supporting-no-kings-protest-and-it-becomes-global-how-travel-gets-impact-this-weekend/ |access-date=2025-06-20 |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-06-15 |title=No Kings: protests in the eye of the storm |url=https://www.theverge.com/policy/687195/no-kings-trump-parade-protests |access-date=2025-06-20 |website=The Verge |language=en-US |archive-date=July 27, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250727043743/https://www.theverge.com/policy/687195/no-kings-trump-parade-protests |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[June 16]]–[[June 17|17]] – The [[51st G7 summit]] is held in [[Kananaskis Improvement District|Kananaskis, Canada]].<ref>{{cite web|title=G7 leaders gather in Canada amid Mideast crisis, tariff woes|url=https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20250616-g7-leaders-canada-mideast-tariffs|publisher=France 24|date=June 16, 2025 |access-date=29 August 2025}}</ref>
* [[June 20]] – [[2025 Enderlin tornado|An EF5 tornado]] strikes southeast of [[Enderlin, North Dakota]], becoming the first EF5 tornado globally since [[2013 Moore tornado|May 20, 2013]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Sandoval|first=Tadeo Ruiz|date=2025-10-08|title=Enderlin tornado earns rare EF-5 category after derailing 33 train cars|url=https://www.mprnews.org/story/2025/10/08/enderlin-tornado-earns-rare-ef5-category-after-derailing-33-train-cars |access-date=2025-10-09|website=[[MPR News]]|language=en}}</ref>
* [[June 21]] – Belarusian opposition leader [[Sergei Tikhanovsky]] and 13 other political prisoners are released from prison and deported to Lithuania following a pardon as a result of negotiations with Trump's envoy in Minsk.<ref>{{Cite web |date=21 June 2025 |title=Belarus Opposition Leader Tikhanovsky Freed From Jail |url=https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2025/06/21/belarus-opposition-leader-tikhanovsky-freed-from-jail-a89524 |access-date=21 June 2025 |website=The Moscow Times}}</ref>
* [[June 22]] – [[Twelve-Day War]]: The [[United States]] carries out [[Northrop B-2 Spirit|B-2 bomber]] [[2025 United States strikes on Iranian nuclear sites|airstrikes on three Iranian nuclear sites]] in [[Fordow Uranium Enrichment Plant|Fordow]], [[Natanz Nuclear Facility|Natanz]], and [[Isfahan Nuclear Technology/Research Center|Isfahan]].<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Nagourney |first1=Eric |last2=Haberman |first2=Maggie |date=June 21, 2025 |title=U.S. Enters War With Iran, Striking Fordo Nuclear Site: Live Updates |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2025/06/21/world/iran-israel-trump |access-date=June 21, 2025 |work=The New York Times |issn=0362-4331 |archive-date=June 21, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250621110851/https://www.nytimes.com/live/2025/06/21/world/iran-israel-trump |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[June 23]] – Iran [[2025 Iranian strikes on Al Udeid Air Base|launches missiles at Al Udeid Air Base]] in [[Qatar]] in response to the previous day's U.S. strikes.<ref>{{Cite news |date=June 23, 2025 |title=Iran launches missiles at US bases in Qatar and Iraq in response to strikes, state media reports |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cn7ze4vmk2pt |access-date=June 23, 2025 |work=BBC News |archive-date=June 23, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250623000053/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cn7ze4vmk2pt |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[June 24]]–[[June 25|25]] – A [[2025 The Hague NATO summit|NATO summit]] is held at the [[World Forum (The Hague)|World Forum]] in [[The Hague|The Hague, Netherlands]].<ref>{{cite web|title=NATO summit opens in The Hague amid unprecedented security and protests|url=https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20250624-largest-ever-international-summit-organised-by-the-dutch-opens-in-the-hague|publisher=Radio France Internationale|date=June 24, 2025 |access-date=29 August 2025}}</ref>
* [[June 25]] – The [[Axiom Mission 4]] is launched. The mission involves four astronauts, including the first astronauts from Poland ([[Sławosz Uznański-Wiśniewski]]) and India ([[Shubhanshu Shukla]]) since the end of the [[Cold War]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Sławosz Uznański-Wiśniewski już na ISS. Polski astronauta zabrał głos |url=https://wiadomosci.onet.pl/kraj/slawosz-uznanski-wisniewski-juz-na-iss-polski-astronauta-zabral-glos/m3t4ybg |publisher=Onet |access-date=27 June 2025 |language=pl |date=26 June 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=25 June 2025 |title=India, Poland and Hungary make spaceflight comeback with ISS mission |url=https://www.theguardian.com/science/2025/jun/25/india-poland-hungary-us-astronauts-iss-axiom-mission-4 |access-date=27 June 2025 |work=The Guardian |language=en |archive-date=August 6, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250806091247/https://www.theguardian.com/science/2025/jun/25/india-poland-hungary-us-astronauts-iss-axiom-mission-4 |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[June 27]] – The U.S., with Qatari support, brokers a preliminary [[2025 Democratic Republic of the Congo–Rwanda peace agreement|peace treaty]] between the [[Democratic Republic of the Congo]] and [[Rwanda]], ending [[Democratic Republic of the Congo–Rwanda conflict (2022–present)|their armed conflict]] that started in 2022.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Psaledakis |first1=Daphne |last2=Rolley |first2=Sonia |last3=Kasongo |first3=Ange Adihe |last4=Psaledakis |first4=Daphne |date=2025-06-27 |title=Rwanda, Congo sign peace deal in US to end fighting, attract investment |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/rwanda-democratic-republic-congo-set-sign-peace-agreement-washington-2025-06-27/ |access-date=2025-06-27 |work=Reuters |language=en |archive-date=June 27, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250627195136/https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/rwanda-democratic-republic-congo-set-sign-peace-agreement-washington-2025-06-27/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

=== July ===
[[File:Flooding of the Guadalupe River near Kerrville, Texas in 2025.jpg|thumb|Aerial photo of the [[July 2025 Central Texas floods|Central Texas floods]] near [[Hunt, Texas|Hunt]] on July 5]]
[[File:Milestone College 22 July (cropped).jpg|thumb|A fighter jet of [[Bangladesh Air Force]] [[2025 Dhaka Chengdu J-7 crash|crashed]] at [[Milestone College|Milestone School]] on July 22]]
[[File:RA-47315 main wreckage (1) (cropped).jpg|thumb|The wreckage of [[Angara Airlines Flight 2311]] near the Eastern Siberian city of [[Tynda]], Amur Oblast, Russia]]
* [[July 1]] – [[2025 Thai political crisis]]: The [[Constitutional Court of Thailand]] suspends [[Prime Minister of Thailand|Prime Minister]] [[Paetongtarn Shinawatra]] from duty pending a case seeking her dismissal.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Saksornchai {{!}} AP |first=Jintamas |date=2025-07-01 |title=Court suspends Thailand's Prime Minister Paetongtarn Shinawatra to investigate leaked phone call |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2025/07/01/thailand-cabinet-paetongtarn-leak-call-cambodia/2523a636-5638-11f0-b45b-dc9aeb848c03_story.html |access-date=2025-07-01 |newspaper=The Washington Post |language=en-US |issn=0190-8286 |archive-date=July 1, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250701075459/https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2025/07/01/thailand-cabinet-paetongtarn-leak-call-cambodia/2523a636-5638-11f0-b45b-dc9aeb848c03_story.html |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[July 4]]–[[July 7|7]] – At least 135 people are killed and over a hundred reported missing during a [[July 2025 Central Texas floods|flood in Central Texas]], United States.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2025/07/07/us/texas-floods |title=Texas Flood Live Updates: Summer Camp Says 27 Girls and Staff Killed, With 11 Still Missing |date=7 July 2025 |work=The New York Times |accessdate=7 July 2025 |archive-date=July 23, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250723183710/https://www.nytimes.com/live/2025/07/07/us/texas-floods |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[July 11]] – [[August 3]] – The [[2025 World Aquatics Championships]] are held in [[Singapore]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.worldaquatics.com/competitions/4725/world-aquatics-championships-singapore-2025|title=World Aquatics Championships - Singapore 2025|publisher=World Aquatics |access-date=December 31, 2024|archive-date=December 31, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241231135421/https://www.worldaquatics.com/competitions/4725/world-aquatics-championships-singapore-2025|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[July 13]] – Several [[Southern Syria clashes (July 2025–present)|clashes]] erupt in southern Syria between armed [[Druze]] and [[Bedouin]] groups.<ref>{{cite news |title=توتر متصاعد في السويداء.. اشتباكات في حي المقوس وقطع طريق دمشق – السويداء إثر احتجازات متبادلة بين مسلحين محليين وعشائر في المنطقة |trans-title=Rising tension in Suwayda: Clashes in al-Maqwas and Damascus–Suwayda road cut off after mutual detentions between local gunmen and tribes |url=https://www.syriahr.com/%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%AA%D8%B1-%D9%85%D8%AA%D8%B5%D8%A7%D8%B9%D8%AF-%D9%81%D9%8A-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B3%D9%88%D9%8A%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%A1-%D8%A7%D8%B4%D8%AA%D8%A8%D8%A7%D9%83%D8%A7%D8%AA-%D9%81%D9%8A-%D8%AD%D9%8A/769644/ |website=[[Syrian Observatory for Human Rights]] |language=ar |date=13 July 2025 |access-date=16 July 2025 |archive-date=November 27, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251127074603/https://www.syriahr.com/%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%AA%D8%B1-%D9%85%D8%AA%D8%B5%D8%A7%D8%B9%D8%AF-%D9%81%D9%8A-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B3%D9%88%D9%8A%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%A1-%D8%A7%D8%B4%D8%AA%D8%A8%D8%A7%D9%83%D8%A7%D8%AA-%D9%81%D9%8A-%D8%AD%D9%8A/769644/ |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[July 16]] – Israeli [[July 2025 Damascus airstrikes|airstrikes]] hit the [[Presidential Palace, Damascus|Syrian Presidential Palace]] and the [[Hay'at al-Arkan|Syrian General Staff headquarters]] in Damascus.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://news.sky.com/story/israel-attacks-syrian-military-hq-in-damascus-and-issues-warning-to-leave-religious-minority-group-alone-13397411 |title=Israel attacks Syrian military HQ - and disrupts live TV broadcast |date=16 July 2025 |publisher=Sky News|accessdate=16 July 2025}}</ref>
* [[July 21]]
**[[2025 Dhaka Chengdu J-7 crash]]: An [[Chengdu J-7|F-7 BGI]] training aircraft of the [[Bangladesh Air Force]] crashes into [[Milestone College]] in [[Uttara (neighbourhood)|Uttara]], [[Dhaka]], killing 31 people including the pilot.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-07-21 |title=Bangladesh crash: At least 19 dead after air force jet crashes into school |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c75rprqwr67o |access-date=2025-07-21 |publisher=BBC |language=en-GB |archive-date=July 26, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250726195040/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c75rprqwr67o |url-status=live }}</ref>
**Twenty-eight countries issue a joint statement calling for an immediate end to the [[Gaza war]], saying it has "reached new depths" in terms of the suffering of civilians.<ref>{{Cite web |first=David |last=Gritten |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4g814gy2e7o |title=Gaza: UK and 27 other nations condemn Israel over civilian suffering |date=21 July 2025 |website=BBC News |publisher=BBC |accessdate=22 July 2025 |archive-date=July 22, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250722085245/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4g814gy2e7o |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[July 23]] – The [[International Court of Justice]] (ICJ) rules that countries can sue each other over historical emissions of [[greenhouse gases]] and the [[effects of climate change]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ce379k4v3pwo |title=Top UN court says countries can sue each other over climate change |date=23 July 2025 |website=BBC News|publisher=BBC |accessdate=24 July 2025}}</ref>
* [[July 24]] 
**[[Angara Airlines Flight 2311]], operated by an [[Antonov An-24]] aircraft, crashes near [[Tynda]] in Eastern Siberia, Russia. All 48 people on board are killed.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Osborn |first1=Andrew |last2=Stolyarov |first2=Gleb |date=24 July 2025 |title=Russian plane crashes in Russia's far east, nearly 50 people on board feared dead |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/aerospace-defense/russian-plane-missing-with-around-50-people-board-amur-region-interfax-says-2025-07-24/ |access-date=24 July 2025 |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref>
**Armed [[2025 Cambodia–Thailand border conflict|conflicts]] break out between [[Cambodia]] and [[Thailand]] after the escalation of a border dispute. At least 39 people are killed and more than 100,000 displaced due to the conflicts.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-07-25 |title=Thailand-Cambodia military exchanges could lead to war, acting Thai PM says |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-07-25/thailand-cambodia-border-conflict-calls-for-peace/105570648 |access-date=2025-07-26 |work=ABC News |language=en-AU |archive-date=July 27, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250727195741/https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-07-25/thailand-cambodia-border-conflict-calls-for-peace/105570648 |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[July 30]] – An {{M|w|link=y}} [[2025 Kamchatka Peninsula earthquake|8.8 earthquake]] strikes off the coast of Russia's [[Kamchatka Peninsula]], triggering tsunami warnings in [[Japan]] and [[Hawaii]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Powerful quake in Russia's Far East causes tsunami, Japan and Hawaii order evacuations |work=Reuters |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/environment/magnitude-8-earthquake-strikes-off-russias-kamchatka-sparks-tsunamis-warnings-2025-07-29/ |access-date=30 July 2025}}</ref>

=== August ===
[[File:Trump, Putin Alaska Arrival (9260673).jpg|thumb|[[Vladimir Putin]] and [[Donald Trump]] arriving in [[Anchorage, Alaska]], for the [[2025 Russia–United States Summit|Russia–United States Summit]] on August 15]]
* [[August 7]]–[[August 17|17]] – The [[2025 World Games]] are held in [[Chengdu]], China.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.theworldgames.org/editions/Your-City-Your-Country-2025-14|title=TWG 2025 Chengdu, CHN|publisher=The World Games|access-date=December 31, 2024|archive-date=December 31, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241231135421/https://www.theworldgames.org/editions/Your-City-Your-Country-2025-14|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[August 7]] – [[OpenAI]]'s model [[GPT-5]] is released.<ref>{{cite web|last=Milmo|first=Dan|title=OpenAI says latest ChatGPT upgrade is big step forward but still can't do humans' jobs|url=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2025/aug/07/openai-chatgpt-upgrade-big-step-forward-human-jobs-gpt-5|work=The Guardian|date=August 7, 2025 |access-date=8 August 2025}}</ref>
* [[August 8]] – [[Armenia]] and [[Azerbaijan]] sign a [[Armenia–Azerbaijan peace agreement|peace deal]] to end 37-year-old hostilities regarding the [[Nagorno-Karabakh conflict]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=9 August 2025 |title=Azerbaijan and Armenia sign peace deal at White House that creates a 'Trump Route' in region |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/aug/09/azerbaijan-and-armenia-sign-peace-deal-at-white-house-that-creates-a-trump-route-in-region |work=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref>
* [[August 15]] – [[2025 Russia–United States Summit]]: US president Donald Trump meets with Russian president Vladimir Putin in [[Anchorage, Alaska]], to discuss a plan for resolving the [[Russo-Ukrainian war (2022–present)|Russo-Ukrainian war]].<ref>{{cite web|last1=Ramaswamy|first1=Swapna Venugopal|last2=Vanden Brook|first2=Tom|title=Trump-Putin meeting: Sprawling Army base that has hosted dignitaries is backdrop for talks|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2025/08/13/trump-putin-meeting-location-joint-base-elmendorf-richardson/85639795007/|work=USA Today|access-date=16 August 2025|archive-date=August 16, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250816000407/https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2025/08/13/trump-putin-meeting-location-joint-base-elmendorf-richardson/85639795007/|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[August 15]]–[[August 17|17]] – The first [[World Humanoid Robot Games]] are held in [[Beijing]], [[China]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Hawkins |first=Amy |date=2025-08-15 |title=Box, run, crash: China's humanoid robot games show advances and limitations |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/aug/15/china-world-humanoid-robot-games-advances-limitations |access-date=2025-08-19 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Photos: Humanoid robots race and tumble at China's first 'robot Olympics' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/gallery/2025/8/18/humanoid-robots-race-tumble-at-chinas-first-robot-olympics |access-date=2025-08-19 |publisher=Al Jazeera |language=en |archive-date=September 20, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250920171903/https://www.aljazeera.com/gallery/2025/8/18/humanoid-robots-race-tumble-at-chinas-first-robot-olympics |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[August 19]] – A [[2025 Herat road crash|multi-vehicle collision]] involving a bus carrying [[2025 Afghan deportation from Iran|migrants deported from Iran]], a motorcycle and a truck kills at least 79 people in [[Herat Province]], [[Afghanistan]].<ref>{{cite web|last=Ewe|first=Koh|title=Dozens of Afghan deportees from Iran killed in bus crash|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c336jj5xkvko|publisher=BBC|date=August 20, 2025|access-date=27 August 2025|archive-date=October 9, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251009154455/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c336jj5xkvko|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[August 22]] – [[Gaza Strip famine|Famine]] is confirmed in [[Gaza City]] for the first time after the UN-backed body responsible for monitoring food security raises its classification to [[Integrated Food Security Phase Classification|Phase 5]], the highest and worst level. The IPC says more than 500,000 people are now facing "starvation, destitution and death".<ref>{{cite web|title=Famine confirmed in Gaza City for first time, UN-backed report says|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/ckgj0yn3dzjt|work=BBC News|date=22 August 2025|access-date=22 August 2025}}</ref>
* [[August 22]] – [[September 27]] – The [[2025 Women's Rugby World Cup]] is held in, and [[2025 Women's Rugby World Cup final|is won]] by, [[England women's national rugby union team|England]].<ref>{{cite web|last1=Rendell |first1=Sarah |title=England outclass Canada to capture glorious Women's Rugby World Cup triumph|url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/sep/27/england-outclass-canada-to-capture-glorious-womens-rugby-world-cup-triumph|work=The Guardian|date=September 27, 2025 |access-date=27 September 2025}}</ref>
* [[August 30]] – [[2025 Thai political crisis]]: The [[Constitutional Court of Thailand]] removes [[Prime Minister of Thailand|Prime Minister]] [[Paetongtarn Shinawatra]] from office for ethical misconduct over [[Thailand–Cambodia phone call leak|leaked phone calls]] she had with former [[Prime Minister of Cambodia|Cambodian Prime Minister]] [[Hun Sen]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/8/29/thai-court-removes-prime-minister-paetongtarn-shinawatra-from-office | title=Thai court removes Prime Minister Paetongtarn Shinawatra from office | publisher=Al Jazeera | date=29 August 2025 | access-date=29 August 2025 | archive-date=September 2, 2025 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250902092852/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/8/29/thai-court-removes-prime-minister-paetongtarn-shinawatra-from-office | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=29 August 2025 |title=Thailand PM Paetongtarn Shinawatra sacked over Cambodia call |url=https://www.dw.com/en/thailand-pm-paetongtarn-shinawatra-sacked-over-cambodia-call/a-73802515 |access-date=29 August 2025 |publisher=[[Deutsche Welle]] |language=en |archive-date=August 29, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250829142551/https://www.dw.com/en/thailand-pm-paetongtarn-shinawatra-sacked-over-cambodia-call/a-73802515 |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[August 31]] 
** An [[2025 Kunar earthquake|earthquake]] in eastern [[Afghanistan]] kills over 2,200 people and injures 3,500.<ref>{{cite web|title=Afghan survivors struggle in the wake of deadly earthquake|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/9/6/afghan-survivors-struggle-in-the-wake-of-deadly-earthquake|publisher=Al Jazeera|access-date=7 September 2025|archive-date=September 8, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250908230632/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/9/6/afghan-survivors-struggle-in-the-wake-of-deadly-earthquake|url-status=live}}</ref>
** Between 370 and 1,000 people are reported killed in a [[2025 Tarasin landslide|landslide]] caused by heavy rain that buries the village of Tarasin in the [[Marrah Mountains]] of [[Central Darfur]] and leaves one survivor.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-09-03 |title=Race to find survivors after Sudan landslide kills hundreds |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cdj2jygzzk9o |access-date=2025-09-03 |publisher=BBC |language=en |archive-date=September 2, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250902025141/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cdj2jygzzk9o |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-09-01 |title=Landslide wipes out entire village in Central Darfur's Jebel Marra |url=https://sudantribune.com/article304586/ |access-date=2025-09-02 |work=Sudan Tribune |language=en |archive-date=September 2, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250902112852/https://sudantribune.com/article304586/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

=== September ===
