* [[September 3]] – At least 16 people are killed and over 21 are injured after the [[Ascensor da Glória derailment|Glória funicular derailment]] in the centre of [[Lisbon]], [[Portugal]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=September 3, 2025 |title=What we know about fatal Lisbon funicular derailment |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn95l12epxzo |access-date=September 3, 2025 |work=[[BBC News]] |archive-date=September 3, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250903215600/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn95l12epxzo |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|date=September 4, 2025|title=Elevador da Glória. Proteção Civil corrige número de mortos para 16|url=https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/pais/elevador-da-gloria-numero-de-mortos-sobe-para-17_n1681247|publisher=[[Rádio e Televisão de Portugal|RTP]]|language=pt|archive-date=September 4, 2025|access-date=September 4, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250904232017/https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/pais/elevador-da-gloria-numero-de-mortos-sobe-para-17_n1681247|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[September 8]]
**[[2025 Norwegian parliamentary election]]: Incumbent Prime Minister [[Jonas Gahr Støre]]'s coalition retains their majority.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Bryant |first1=Miranda |title=Norway's Labour party wins election after seeing off populist surge|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/08/norways-labour-party-holds-narrow-lead-in-early-election-results|work=The Guardian|date=September 8, 2025 |access-date=9 September 2025}}</ref>
**[[2024–2025 French political crisis]]: The [[Bayrou government]] collapses after losing a [[no-confidence vote]].<ref>{{cite web|title=French government collapses as MPs vote to oust prime minister|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/c5yqgnzw759t|work=BBC News|date=8 September 2025|access-date=8 September 2025|archive-date=September 8, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250908175148/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/c5yqgnzw759t|url-status=live}}</ref>
**[[2025 Nepalese Gen Z protests|Mass anti-government protests]] erupt in [[Nepal]], resulting in at least 22 deaths and hundreds injured. [[Prime Minister of Nepal|Prime Minister]] [[K. P. Sharma Oli]] resigns the following day amidst the demonstrations.<ref>{{cite web|last=Mohamed|first=Edna|title=Nepal protests updates: PM Oli resigns, parliament torched, airport shut|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2025/9/9/nepal-protests-live-nepali-congress-office-top-leaders-homes-set-on-fire|publisher=Al Jazeera|access-date=10 September 2025|archive-date=September 13, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913183308/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2025/9/9/nepal-protests-live-nepali-congress-office-top-leaders-homes-set-on-fire|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[September 9]]
**The [[Eightieth session of the United Nations General Assembly|80th session]] of the [[United Nations General Assembly]] opens in [[New York City]], [[United States]].<ref>{{cite web|last=Stepansky|first=Joseph|title='Illusions stripped away': What to know about the 80th UN General Assembly|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/9/9/illusions-stripped-away-what-to-know-about-the-80th-un-general-assembly|publisher=Al Jazeera|access-date=10 September 2025|archive-date=September 12, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250912144124/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/9/9/illusions-stripped-away-what-to-know-about-the-80th-un-general-assembly|url-status=live}}</ref>
**Israel [[Israeli airstrike on Hamas leadership in Qatar|attacks]] the [[Hamas]] leadership in [[Doha]], [[Qatar]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/9/9/israeli-military-says-it-has-attacked-hamas-leadership-in-qatars-doha |title=Israeli military says it attacked Hamas leaders in Qatar's Doha |publisher=Al Jazeera |date=9 September 2025 |archive-date=December 7, 2025 |access-date=September 10, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251207232154/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/9/9/israeli-military-says-it-has-attacked-hamas-leadership-in-qatars-doha |url-status=live }}</ref>
**[[September 2025 Russian drone incursion into Poland|Russian drone incursion into Poland]]: Multiple drones breach Polish airspace during a large-scale Russian attack on Ukraine and are intercepted by Polish and NATO forces, marking the first attack on [[NATO]] territory and prompting Poland to invoke [[Article 4 of the North Atlantic Treaty|Article 4]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Poland closer to conflict than any time since second world war, PM says, as Russia claims drone incursion was unintentional – live |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2025/sep/10/poland-pm-condemns-repeated-violation-of-airspace-amid-russian-attack-on-ukraine-follow-live|work=The Guardian|date=10 September 2025|access-date=10 September 2025}}</ref>
* [[September 10]]
**A [[Liquefied petroleum gas|liquid petroleum gas]] truck [[2025 Iztapalapa tank truck explosion|overturns and explodes]] at an overpass in [[Iztapalapa]], [[Mexico City]], killing 32 people and injuring 90 others.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.macaubusiness.com/death-toll-in-mexico-city-gas-truck-blast-climbs-to-29/|title=Death toll in Mexico City gas truck blast climbs to 29|agency=Agence France-Presse|date=25 September 2025|website=Macau Business|access-date=22 September 2025}}</ref>
**[[Charlie Kirk]], an American right-wing activist and influential ally of [[Donald Trump|President Trump]], is [[assassination of Charlie Kirk|assassinated]] at a campus event in [[Utah]], prompting widespread reactions and [[Reprisals against commentators on the Charlie Kirk assassination|reprisals]] both domestically and internationally.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-09-10 |title=Donald Trump asks for prayers for Charlie Kirk after rightwing activist was shot at Utah university event – latest updates |url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2025/sep/10/donald-trump-jeffrey-epstein-tariffs-immigration-crime-us-politics-live-news-updates |access-date=2025-09-10 |work=The Guardian|language=en}}</ref>
* [[September 11]] – The [[Supreme Federal Court]] [[AP 2668|convicts]] former [[President of Brazil|Brazilian president]] [[Jair Bolsonaro]] and sentences him to 27 years in prison for his involvement in the [[2022 Brazilian coup plot]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://noticias.stf.jus.br/postsnoticias/ap-2668-relator-vota-pela-condenacao-de-todos-os-reus-do-nucleo-1/ | title=AP 2668: relator vota pela condenação de todos os réus do Núcleo 1 | language=pt-br | trans-title=AP 2668: rapporteur votes to convict all eight defendants of Group 1 | website=[[Supreme Federal Court]] | date=2025-09-09 | access-date=2025-09-10 | archive-date=September 10, 2025 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250910151650/https://noticias.stf.jus.br/postsnoticias/ap-2668-relator-vota-pela-condenacao-de-todos-os-reus-do-nucleo-1/ | url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-09-11 |title=Bolsonaro sentenced to 27 years in prison for plotting Brazil coup |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c8xrqxk9p4xo |access-date=2025-09-11 |website=BBC News |language=en-GB |archive-date=September 11, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250911232140/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c8xrqxk9p4xo |url-status=live }}</ref>
*[[September 12]] – Former [[Chief Justice of Nepal|chief justice]] [[Sushila Karki]] assumes office as [[Prime Minister of Nepal|interim prime minister]] of an [[Interim government of Sushila Karki|interim government]] formed after [[K. P. Sharma Oli]]'s resignation in [[Nepal]],<ref>{{cite web | url = https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/nepal-pm-kp-oli-resigns-after-violent-anti-corruption-protests-report-101757407595025.html | title = Nepal PM KP Oli resigns after violent anti-corruption protests: Report | website = Hindustan Times | date = 9 September 2025 | access-date = 9 September 2025 | archive-date = September 13, 2025 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20250913183353/https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/nepal-pm-kp-oli-resigns-after-violent-anti-corruption-protests-report-101757407595025.html | url-status = live }}</ref> the decision notably being decided via a poll on a social media platform, [[Discord]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-09-11 |title=Nepal's Social Media Ban Backfires as Politics Moves to a Chat Room |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/09/11/world/asia/nepal-protest-genz-discord.html |access-date=2025-09-13 |language=en |archive-date=September 11, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250911224916/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/09/11/world/asia/nepal-protest-genz-discord.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-09-13 |title=How Gen Z protestors chose Nepal's first woman prime minister on Discord |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/asia/nepal-sushila-karki-prime-minister-discord-protests-b2825843.html |access-date=2025-09-13 |website=The Independent |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-09-13 |title=Nepal's Gen Z chooses Discord to 'elect' interim PM: What is this app and how it works |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/technology/tech-news/nepals-gen-z-chooses-discord-to-elect-interim-pm-what-is-this-app-and-how-it-works/articleshow/123867797.cms |access-date=2025-09-13 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257}}</ref>
* [[September 12]]–[[September 28|28]] – The [[2025 FIVB Men's Volleyball World Championship]] is held in [[Pasay]] and [[Quezon City]], the [[Philippines]], and is won by [[Italy men's national volleyball team|Italy]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Italy Crowned 2025 Volleyball World Champions|url=https://worldofvolley.com/latest_news/fivb/331874/italy-crowned-2025-volleyball-world-champions.html|website=WorldofVolley|year=2025|access-date=29 September 2025}}</ref>
* [[September 13]]–[[September 21|21]] – The [[2025 World Athletics Championships]] are held in [[Tokyo]], Japan.<ref>{{cite web|title=Everything you need to know about the 2025 World Athletics Championships in Tokyo|url=https://www.espn.com/olympics/story/_/id/46140438/world-athletics-championships-2025-tokyo-japan-how-watch-australia-gout-gout-nina-kennedy-medals|publisher=ESPN|access-date=13 September 2025|archive-date=September 13, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250913151101/https://www.espn.com/olympics/story/_/id/46140438/world-athletics-championships-2025-tokyo-japan-how-watch-australia-gout-gout-nina-kennedy-medals|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[September 16]]
**[[2025 Malawian general election]]: [[Peter Mutharika]] is elected [[President of Malawi|president]] for a second non-consecutive term.<ref>{{cite web|last=Maseko|first=Nomsa|title=Malawi's ex-president wins election in comeback at age 85|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg4n0rrn1no|publisher=BBC|date=September 25, 2025|access-date=25 September 2025|archive-date=October 3, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251003005347/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg4n0rrn1no|url-status=live}}</ref>
**A [[2025 UNHRC Commission of Inquiry report on Gaza genocide|UN Human Rights Council commission of inquiry]] finds that Israel has committed [[Gaza genocide|genocide against Palestinians in Gaza]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-09-16 |title=Israel has committed genocide in Gaza, UN commission of inquiry says |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c8641wv0n4go |access-date=2025-09-16 |work=BBC News|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-09-16 |title=Gaza: Top independent rights probe alleges Israel committed genocide |url=https://news.un.org/en/story/2025/09/1165856 |access-date=2025-09-16 |work=UN |language=en |archive-date=November 25, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251125205256/https://news.un.org/en/story/2025/09/1165856 |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[September 19]] – [[Estonia]]n airspace near [[Vaindloo]] island is violated by three [[Russia]]n [[Mikoyan MiG-31|MiG-31]] jets. In response, Estonia invokes [[Article 4 of the North Atlantic Treaty|Article 4 of NATO]].<ref>{{Cite news|last1=Sytus|first1=Andrius|last2=Slattery|first2=Gram|date=September 19, 2025 |title=Russian jets enter Estonia's airspace in latest test for NATO |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/aerospace-defense/nato-member-estonia-says-three-russian-jets-violated-its-airspace-2025-09-19/ |access-date=2025-10-15 |work=Reuters}}</ref>
* [[September 20]] – [[Intervision 2025]] is held in [[Moscow]], Russia. [[Vietnam]]ese contestant [[Đức Phúc]] wins with the song "{{lang|vi|[[Phù Đổng Thiên Vương (song)|Phù Đổng Thiên Vương]]|i=unset}}".<ref>{{Cite web|last=Pleitgen|first=Frederik|date=21 September 2025|title=Vietnam's Duc Phuc wins Intervision, Russia's family-friendly answer to the Eurovision|url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/09/20/world/duc-phuc-intervision-russian-song-contest-latam-intl|access-date=21 September 2025|publisher=[[CNN]]|language=en|archive-date=September 24, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250924141404/https://www.cnn.com/2025/09/20/world/duc-phuc-intervision-russian-song-contest-latam-intl|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[September 21]] 
** The [[United Kingdom|UK]], [[Canada]], and [[Australia]] announce their formal [[International recognition of Palestine|recognition of Palestine]] as a sovereign state, with [[France]] also doing so the next day.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-09-21 |title=UK, Canada and Australia announce formal recognition of Palestinian state |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cpw1qkyke4nt |access-date=2025-09-21 |work=BBC News |language=en |archive-date=November 28, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251128085503/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cpw1qkyke4nt |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-09-22|title=France becomes latest nation to recognise Palestinian state|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cpw1qkyke4nt?post=asset%3A98abf853-7f15-43f9-be57-8b3c7d692f5b#post|access-date=2025-09-23|work=BBC News|language=en|archive-date=September 23, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250923124227/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cpw1qkyke4nt?post=asset:98abf853-7f15-43f9-be57-8b3c7d692f5b#post|url-status=live}}</ref>
** [[2025–2026 Philippine anti-corruption protests|Thousands of protesters across the Philippines]] gather at the [[EDSA Shrine]] in Quezon City for the [[Trillion Peso March]] and at [[Rizal Park|Luneta Park]] in Manila for the [[Baha sa Luneta]] demonstrations, demanding government accountability over [[Flood control projects scandal in the Philippines|alleged corruption in flood control and infrastructure projects]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Chi|first=Cristina|date=September 15, 2025|title=What to Know: September 21 anti-corruption rallies at Luneta, EDSA|url=https://www.philstar.com/headlines/2025/09/15/2473004/what-know-september-21-anti-corruption-rallies-luneta-edsa|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250921073541/https://www.philstar.com/headlines/2025/09/15/2473004/what-know-september-21-anti-corruption-rallies-luneta-edsa|archive-date=September 21, 2025|access-date=September 18, 2025|newspaper=[[Philippine Daily Inquirer]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last1=Ratcliffe |first1=Rebecca |date=September 21, 2025 |title=Protesters Flood Streets of Philippines Over State Corruption |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/21/protests-philippines-corruption-state-flood |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250922163446/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/sep/21/protests-philippines-corruption-state-flood |archive-date=September 22, 2025 |access-date=September 21, 2025 |website=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref>
* [[September 27]] – [[2025 Karur crowd crush]]: At least 40 people are killed and 51 injured in a crowd crush at a rally held by actor-turned-politician [[C. Joseph Vijay|Vijay]]'s party [[Tamilaga Vettri Kazhagam]] (TVK) in [[Karur]], [[Tamil Nadu]], India.<ref>{{Cite news |date=28 September 2025 |title=At least 40 dead in crush at political rally in India |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c98dqyj5dpjo |access-date=29 September 2025 |publisher=BBC}}</ref> 
* [[September 28]] – [[2025 Moldovan parliamentary election]]: Incumbent pro-European party [[Party of Action and Solidarity|PAS]] wins reelection, forming another majority government.<ref>{{Cite news|last1=Nicholls|first1=Catherine|last2=Gak|first2=Kosta|last3=Edwards|first3=Christian|last4=Regan|first4=Helen|date=2025-09-29|title=Moldova's ruling pro-EU party wins election marred by claims of Russian meddling|url=https://edition.cnn.com/2025/09/29/europe/moldova-election-eu-russia-intl-hnk|access-date=2025-09-29|publisher=CNN|language=en}}</ref>
* [[September 30]] – A {{M|w|link=y}} [[2025 Cebu earthquake|6.9 earthquake]] shakes the island of [[Cebu]] in the Philippines, leaving 71 people dead and 559 injured.<ref>{{Cite report |date=2025-10-04 |title=Situational Report No. 5 for the Effects of Magnitude 6.9 Earthquake in Bogo City, Cebu (2025) |url=https://monitoring-dashboard.ndrrmc.gov.ph/assets/uploads/situations/Situational_Report_No__5_for_the_Effects_of_Magnitude_6_9_Earthquake_in_Bogo_City,_Cebu__2025__summary.pdf |access-date=2025-10-04 |website=NDRRMC |language=en }}{{Dead link|date=March 2026 |bot=InternetArchiveBot }}</ref>

