** [[Henri, Grand Duke of Luxembourg]], [[Abdication of Henri, Grand Duke of Luxembourg|abdicates the throne]] in favor of his son [[Guillaume V, Grand Duke of Luxembourg|Guillaume]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20251003-luxembourg-gets-new-grand-duke-with-royal-abdication |title=EU-member Luxembourg enthrones monarch, drawing hundreds |date=3 October 2025 |access-date=3 October 2025 |publisher=France 24 |archive-date=October 4, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251004000339/https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20251003-luxembourg-gets-new-grand-duke-with-royal-abdication |url-status=live }}</ref> 
** [[Sarah Mullally|Dame Sarah Mullally]] is named the first female [[Archbishop of Canterbury]].<ref>{{Cite web |first1=Aleem |last1=Maqbool |first2=Paul |last2=Gribben |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c2lxyxqzxkdo |title=Sarah Mullally named as new Archbishop of Canterbury |date=3 October 2025 |website=BBC News |publisher=BBC |accessdate=3 October 2025 |archive-date=October 5, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251005190915/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c2lxyxqzxkdo |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[October 3]]–[[October 4|4]] – [[2025 Czech parliamentary election]]: [[ANO (political party)|ANO]] leader and former Prime Minister [[Andrej Babiš]] wins a plurality of seats, but fails to reach a majority. Incumbent Prime Minister [[Petr Fiala]]'s coalition fails to win a majority.<ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-10-04|title=Andrej Babiš' ANO movement wins Czech parliamentary elections|url=https://www.euronews.com/2025/10/04/andrej-babis-ano-movement-set-to-win-czech-parliamentary-elections|access-date=2025-10-04|work=Euronews|language=en}}</ref>
* [[October 5]] – The [[2025 Syrian parliamentary election]] is held, the first since the [[fall of the Assad regime]] in 2024.<ref>{{Cite news|last=Mallinder|first=Lorraine|date=2025-10-06|title=Syria shares results of parliamentary election amid inclusivity concerns|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/10/6/syria-declares-results-of-1st-parliamentary-poll-amid-inclusivity-concerns|access-date=2025-10-08|publisher=Al Jazeera|language=en}}</ref>
* [[October 9]]
** Israel and Hamas agree to the first phase of a [[Gaza war|Gaza]] [[Gaza peace plan|peace deal]], paving the way for a ceasefire, almost exactly two years after the [[Gaza War|conflict]] began.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-10-09 |title=Trump says Israel and Hamas have agreed to first phase of Gaza peace deal, paving way for ceasefire |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cx2nzlj2j4kt |access-date=2025-10-09 |website=BBC News |language=en-GB |archive-date=October 8, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251008230259/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cx2nzlj2j4kt |url-status=live }}</ref>
** [[2025 Afghanistan–Pakistan conflict]]: Pakistan reportedly carries out airstrikes in [[Kabul]], [[Khost]], [[Jalalabad]], and [[Paktika]], targeting [[Noor Wali Mehsud]], an internationally designated terrorist.<ref>{{Cite news |date=10 October 2025 |title=Mysterious explosions heard in Kabul: Did Pakistan carry out airstrike? Here's what we know |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/mysterious-explosions-heard-in-kabul-did-pakistan-carry-out-airstrike-heres-what-we-know/articleshow/124445121.cms |access-date=10 October 2025 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257 |archive-date=January 4, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260104145220/https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/mysterious-explosions-heard-in-kabul-did-pakistan-carry-out-airstrike-heres-what-we-know/articleshow/124445121.cms |url-status=live }}</ref> 
