**[[Sanae Takaichi]] becomes the first female [[Prime Minister of Japan]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-10-21 |title=Sanae Takaichi makes history as Japan's first female prime minister |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c751z23n3n7o |access-date=2025-10-21 |website=BBC News |language=en-GB |archive-date=October 23, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251023001909/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c751z23n3n7o |url-status=live }}</ref>
**American [[Eric Lu]] wins the quinquennial [[XIX International Chopin Piano Competition]] at the [[National Philharmonic, Warsaw|National Philharmonic]] in [[Warsaw]], [[Poland]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-10-21 |title=Eric Lu wins the 19th Chopin Competition! |url=https://www.chopincompetition.pl/en/newsroom/eric-lu-wins-the-19th-chopin-competition?id=131&type=news |access-date=2025-10-21 |website=Chopin Competition|language=en}}</ref>
* [[October 24]] – [[2025 Irish presidential election]]: Independent candidate [[Catherine Connolly]] wins the election in a landslide, defeating [[Fine Gael]] candidate [[Heather Humphreys]].<ref>{{Cite web|date=2025-10-25|title=Leftwinger Catherine Connolly wins Ireland presidential election by landslide|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/oct/25/catherine-connolly-ireland-presidential-election-leftwing|access-date=2025-10-25|website=The Guardian|language=en}}</ref>
* [[October 26]]
** [[2025 Argentine legislative election]]: Incumbent [[President of Argentina|President]] [[Javier Milei]]'s party [[La Libertad Avanza]] wins the election with over 40% of the votes.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Debre|first=Isabel|date=2025-10-27|title=Milei triumphs in Argentine midterm elections closely watched by Washington|url=https://apnews.com/article/argentina-midterm-election-javier-milei-66d7c03825a7a0f56ce5808ff3ac1df4|access-date=2025-10-27|website=AP News|language=en|archive-date=October 26, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251026234012/https://apnews.com/article/argentina-midterm-election-javier-milei-66d7c03825a7a0f56ce5808ff3ac1df4|url-status=live}}</ref>
** [[Accession of Timor-Leste to ASEAN|Timor-Leste becomes the 11th member state of ASEAN]], being the first enlargement of ASEAN since [[Cambodia]]'s entry in 1999 and comprising all countries of [[Southeast Asia]].<ref>{{Cite web|date=2025-10-25|title=Timor-Leste joins ASEAN, boosting regional unity and peace|url=https://en.antaranews.com/news/387969/timor-leste-joins-asean-boosting-regional-unity-and-peace|access-date=2025-10-26|website=Antara|language=en|archive-date=October 27, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251027162605/https://en.antaranews.com/amp/news/387969/timor-leste-joins-asean-boosting-regional-unity-and-peace|url-status=live}}</ref>
