** [[UPS Airlines Flight 2976]], a Honolulu-bound [[McDonnell Douglas MD-11F]], crashes shortly after take-off near [[Louisville Muhammad Ali International Airport]] in Kentucky, United States, killing all three crew members and 12 people on the ground, as well as injuring 22 others.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Swinney |first1=Cody |date=December 25, 2025 |title=Mayor Greenberg confirms 15th UPS crash victim |url=https://www.whas11.com/article/news/national/ups-plane-crash/mayor-greenberg-confirms-ups-crash-victim/417-eca72dde-f9e3-4e34-8bc3-7d1441e53605 |work=WHAS11 |publisher=[[WHAS-TV]] |access-date=January 19, 2026 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251226021825/https://www.whas11.com/article/news/national/ups-plane-crash/mayor-greenberg-confirms-ups-crash-victim/417-eca72dde-f9e3-4e34-8bc3-7d1441e53605 |archive-date=December 26, 2025}}</ref>
* [[November 6]] – [[Khaled El-Enany]] is elected the new Director-General of [[UNESCO]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Toutate |first1=Issam |title=UNESCO Elects Egyptian Archaeologist Khaled El Enany as New Director-General |url=https://www.moroccoworldnews.com/2025/11/266812/unesco-elects-egyptian-archaeologist-khaled-el-enany-as-new-director-general/ |access-date=6 November 2025 |work=[[Morocco World News]] |date=6 November 2025}}</ref>
* [[November 10]]–[[November 21|21]] – The [[2025 United Nations Climate Change Conference|COP30]] summit is held in [[Belém]], [[Brazil]], focusing on the role of the [[Amazon rainforest]] in [[climate action]].<ref>{{Cite news|last=Peixoto|first=Roberto|date=2025-11-10|title=COP30 começa nesta segunda; saiba o que está em jogo e o que esperar da conferência sobre a crise do clima|trans-title=The COP30 begins this Monday; learn what's at stake and what to expect from the climate crisis summit|url=https://g1.globo.com/meio-ambiente/cop-30/noticia/2025/11/10/cop30-comeca-oficialmente-nesta-segunda-saiba-o-que-esta-em-jogo-e-o-que-esperar-da-conferencia-sobre-a-crise-do-clima.ghtml|access-date=2025-11-10|work=[[G1 (website)|G1]]|language=pt|archive-date=November 10, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251110090020/https://g1.globo.com/meio-ambiente/cop-30/noticia/2025/11/10/cop30-comeca-oficialmente-nesta-segunda-saiba-o-que-esta-em-jogo-e-o-que-esperar-da-conferencia-sobre-a-crise-do-clima.ghtml|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[November 10]] – [[2025 Delhi Red Fort blast]]: At least 15 people are killed and more than 20 people are injured in a car explosion near the [[Red Fort]] in [[Delhi]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=17 November 2025 |title=Red Fort blast: Death toll rises to 15 as two more injured succumb in hospital. |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/india/red-fort-blast-death-toll-rises-to-15-as-two-more-injured-succumb-in-hospital/articleshow/125386066.cms?from=mdr |access-date=17 November 2025 |work=The Economic Times}}</ref>
* [[November 11]] – [[2025 Iraqi parliamentary election]]: Incumbent Prime Minister [[Mohammed Shia' al-Sudani]]'s party [[Reconstruction and Development Coalition|RDC]] wins a plurality of seats.<ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-11-12|last1=Solomon|first1=Erika|last2=Hassan|first2=Falih|title=Iraq's Prime Minister Leads in Elections, but May Struggle to Form Government|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/11/12/world/middleeast/iraq-elections.html|access-date=2025-11-14|work=The New York Times|language=en}}</ref>
* [[November 13]] – The [[New Glenn]] rocket booster lands for the first time.<ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-11-14|last1=Gorman|first1=Steve|last2=Roulette|first2=Joey|last3=Skipper|first3=Joe|title=Blue Origin's New Glenn rocket deploys Mars satellites, sticks booster landing|url=https://www.reuters.com/science/blue-origin-launches-new-glenn-rocket-companys-first-nasa-scale-science-mission-2025-11-13/|access-date=2025-11-15|work=Reuters|language=en}}</ref>
* [[November 17]] – Former [[prime minister of Bangladesh]] [[Sheikh Hasina]] is [[Trial of Sheikh Hasina|found guilty]] of crimes against humanity by a [[International Crimes Tribunal (Bangladesh)|Bangladeshi tribunal]] and [[Capital punishment in Bangladesh|sentenced to death]] in absentia.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-11-17 |title=Bangladesh: Sheikh Hasina sentenced to death over student protests |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cpwvg99e8vdo |access-date=2025-11-19 |publisher=BBC |language=en-GB |archive-date=November 17, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251117205201/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cpwvg99e8vdo |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[November 21]] – [[December 7]] – The [[2025 FIFA Futsal Women's World Cup]] is held in the [[Philippines]], and is won by [[Brazil women's national futsal team|Brazil]].<ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-12-07|last=Javier|first=Nikole|title=Brazil beats Portugal to take home first-ever FIFA Futsal Women's World Cup title|url=https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/sports/football/968768/brazil-beats-portugal-to-take-home-first-ever-fifa-futsal-women-s-world-cup-title/story/|access-date=2025-12-08|work=GMA News Online|language=en}}</ref>
* [[November 22]]–[[November 23|23]] – The [[2025 G20 Johannesburg summit|G20 Johannesburg summit]] is held in [[South Africa]], the first time a [[G20]] summit has been held in Africa.<ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-11-22|last=Lawal|first=Shola|title=G20 summit in South Africa: Who's attending and what's on the agenda?|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2025/11/22/g20-summit-in-south-africa-whos-attending-and-whats-on-the-agenda|access-date=2025-11-22|publisher=Al Jazeera|language=en|archive-date=November 22, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251122103741/https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2025/11/22/g20-summit-in-south-africa-whos-attending-and-whats-on-the-agenda|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[November 23]] – [[2025 Guinea-Bissau general election]]: A [[2025 Guinea-Bissau coup d'état|coup d'état]] occurs a day before the official results release, overthrowing President [[Umaro Sissoco Embaló]].<ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-11-23|last=Motamedi|first=Maziar|title=Guinea-Bissau, beset by coups, votes in contentious presidential election|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/11/23/guinea-bissau-beset-by-coups-votes-in-contentious-presidential-election|access-date=2025-11-24|publisher=Al Jazeera|language=en|archive-date=November 28, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251128075813/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/11/23/guinea-bissau-beset-by-coups-votes-in-contentious-presidential-election|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20251126-guinea-bissau-military-claims-to-have-seized-power-after-disputed-vote|title=Guinea-Bissau military claims to have seized power after disputed vote|publisher=Radio France Internationale|date=26 November 2025|access-date=November 28, 2025}}</ref>
* [[November 24]]–[[November 25|25]] – The second round of the [[2025 Egyptian parliamentary election]] is held.<ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-11-27|last=Elmasry|first=Mohamad|title=Egypt's all-important parliamentary elections aren't elections at all|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/opinions/2025/11/27/egypts-all-important-parliamentary-elections-arent-elections-at-all|access-date=2025-12-04|publisher=Al Jazeera|language=en}}</ref>
* [[November 25]] – A report published by the [[United Nations]] shows that [[Indonesia]]n capital [[Jakarta]] has surpassed [[Japan]]ese capital [[Tokyo]] as the world's largest city, with a population of 42 million people.<ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-11-25|last=Ganglani|first=Jay|title=Move aside Tokyo, the world has a new largest city|url=https://www.nbcnews.com/world/asia/jakarta-worlds-largest-city-tokyo-most-populated-dhaka-new-un-report-rcna245798|access-date=2025-11-25|publisher=NBC News|language=en|archive-date=November 25, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251125142414/https://www.nbcnews.com/world/asia/jakarta-worlds-largest-city-tokyo-most-populated-dhaka-new-un-report-rcna245798|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[November 26]] – [[December 14]] – The [[2025 World Women's Handball Championship]] is held in [[Germany]] and the [[Netherlands]], and is won by [[Norway women's national handball team|Norway]].<ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-12-14|last=Frandsen|first=Svend Bertil|title=German fairytale campaign ends in tears as Norway win World Cup final thriller|url=https://www.flashscore.com/news/handball-world-championship-women-german-fairytale-campaign-ends-in-tears-as-norway-win-world-cup-final-thriller/0joDs8Vi/|access-date=2025-12-15|work=Flashscore|language=en}}</ref>
* [[November 26]] 
** A [[Wang Fuk Court fire|massive fire]] engulfs the Wang Fuk Court apartment block in [[Hong Kong]], killing at least {{wikidata|property|references|Q137017220|P1120}} people and leaving over 150 missing.<ref>{{Cite news|title=Hong Kong fire death toll rises to 128 as officials say fire alarms not working properly|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/live/c2emg1kj1klt|publisher=BBC|access-date=November 28, 2025|archive-date=November 26, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251126132304/https://www.bbc.com/news/live/c2emg1kj1klt|url-status=live}}</ref>
** [[Cyclone Senyar]] causes at least 1,390 deaths and leaves 186 missing in [[Thailand]], [[Malaysia]] and [[Indonesia]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Death toll from floods in Thailand reaches 145|url=https://abcnews.go.com/International/wireStory/death-toll-floods-thailand-reach-145-receding-water-127939897|date=28 November 2025|access-date=28 November 2025|newspaper=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]]|archive-date=November 28, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251128120657/https://abcnews.go.com/International/wireStory/death-toll-floods-thailand-reach-145-receding-water-127939897|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|title=Update Banjir-Longsor Sumut: 116 Warga Meninggal, 42 Orang Dalam Pencarian|url=https://nasional.kompas.com/read/2025/11/28/17444331/update-banjir-longsor-sumut-116-warga-meninggal-42-orang-dalam-pencarian.|language=id|date=2 November 2025|access-date=28 November 2025|agency=[[Kompas.com]]}}</ref>
* [[November 27]]–[[November 30|30]] – An [[Ecumenism|ecumenical meeting]] of the [[Eastern Orthodox Church]] and [[Catholic Church]] at [[Nicaea]] [[Visit by Pope Leo XIV to Turkey and Lebanon|is held]] to mark the 1,700th anniversary of the [[First Council of Nicaea]].<ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-11-28|title=Pope Leo XIV begins Turkiye visit with prayers and unity message|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/gallery/2025/11/28/pope-leo-xiv-begins-turkiye-visit-with-prayers-and-unity-message|access-date=2025-12-18|publisher=Al Jazeera|language=en}}</ref>
* [[November 28]] – Flooding and landslides caused by [[Cyclone Ditwah]] leave at least 647 dead and 183 missing across [[Sri Lanka]] and [[South India]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=28 November 2025 |title=Death toll from Sri Lanka landslides and floods rises to 69 |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/11/28/sri-lanka-landslides-floods-death-toll-rises-to-56-offices-schools-shut |access-date=30 November 2025 |publisher=[[Al Jazeera]] |archive-date=December 2, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251202050446/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/11/28/sri-lanka-landslides-floods-death-toll-rises-to-56-offices-schools-shut |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[November 30]] 
** The [[2025 Kyrgyz parliamentary election]] is held.<ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-11-30|last1=Light|first1=Felix|last2=Turgunbaeva|first2=Aigerim|title=Allies of Kyrgyzstan's strongman president sweep snap parliamentary election|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/allies-kyrgyzstans-president-win-majority-parliamentary-election-preliminary-2025-11-30/|access-date=2025-12-01|work=Reuters|language=en}}</ref>
** [[2025 Honduran general election]]: Amid allegations of fraud and external interference, [[National Party of Honduras|National]] candidate [[Nasry Asfura]] narrowly wins the presidency after weeks of delays. The National Party additionally wins a plurality in the [[National Congress of Honduras|National Congress]].<ref>{{Cite news|last=Whitehead|first=Jamie|date=2025-12-24|title=Trump-backed candidate wins in knife-edge Honduran election|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cyvgz1jn368o|access-date=2025-12-25|publisher=BBC|language=en|archive-date=March 19, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260319214649/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cyvgz1jn368o|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== December ===
[[File:Bulgarian protests on 1 December 2025 (12x5 Cropped).png|thumb|[[Largo, Sofia]], during the [[2025 Bulgarian protests|Bulgarian protests]] on December 1]]
[[File:Bondi Beach massacre 004 (flatter cropped).jpg|thumb|Floral tributes and candles to victims of the [[2025 Bondi Beach shooting|Bondi Beach shooting]] on December 14]]
* [[December 2]] – [[Yemeni civil war (2014–present)|Yemeni civil war]]: The [[Southern Transitional Council]] launches a large-scale [[2025 Southern Yemen offensive|military offensive]] across Southern Yemen, breaking years of military stalemate in the conflict.<ref>{{cite news |title=Saudi Arabia says national security is a red line as UAE forces asked to leave Yemen |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/saudi-led-coalition-yemen-calls-civilians-mukalla-port-evacuate-saudi-state-news-2025-12-30/ |access-date=30 December 2025 |publisher=Reuters |date=30 December 2025 |archive-date=January 1, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260101190356/https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/saudi-led-coalition-yemen-calls-civilians-mukalla-port-evacuate-saudi-state-news-2025-12-30/ |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[December 6]] 
**Eleven are killed, including three young children, and fourteen are injured in a [[2025 Saulsville shooting|shooting]] at a bar in [[Saulsville]], Gauteng, South Africa.<ref>{{cite news |last=Kumwenda-Mtambo |first=Olivia |title=Shooting at South African bar leaves 11 dead, including a young child, police say |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/shooting-south-african-bar-leaves-11-dead-including-young-child-police-say-2025-12-06/ |newspaper=Reuters |date=2025-12-06 |access-date=2025-12-06}}</ref>
**A [[2025 Arpora nightclub fire|fire]] at a nightclub in [[Arpora]], [[Goa]], India, leaves at least 25 people dead and 50 injured.<ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-12-06|last=Regencia|first=Ted|title=Nightclub fire in India's Goa kills 25, including four tourists|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/12/6/at-least-23-people-killed-in-nightclub-fire-in-indias-goa|access-date=2025-12-13|publisher=Al Jazeera|language=en|archive-date=December 14, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251214182715/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/12/6/at-least-23-people-killed-in-nightclub-fire-in-indias-goa|url-status=live}}</ref>
*[[December 7]] – Elements of the [[Benin Armed Forces]], led by [[Pascal Tigri]], announce a [[2025 Beninese coup attempt|coup d'état]] against [[President of Benin|president]] [[Patrice Talon]] and the creation of a [[military junta]] after seizing [[Bénin TV|state television]]. However, the coup attempt is thwarted and unsuccessful.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/12/7/soldiers-appear-on-benin-state-television-announcing-apparent-coup|title=Soldiers appear on Benin state television announcing apparent coup|work=[[Al Jazeera]]|date=7 December 2025|access-date=April 2, 2026|archive-date=December 9, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251209193356/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/12/7/soldiers-appear-on-benin-state-television-announcing-apparent-coup|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[December 8]] – A {{M|w|link=y}} [[2025 Sanriku earthquake|7.6 earthquake]] occurs in the [[Pacific Ocean]] off the coast of [[Aomori Prefecture]] in [[Japan]], triggering a [[tsunami]] up to 70&nbsp;cm high.<ref>{{cite anss|M 7.6 - 2025 Aomori Prefecture, Japan Earthquake|2025|pt25342050}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Yamaguchi |first1=Mari |title=Magnitude 7.5 quake in northern Japan injures 23 people and triggers a tsunami |url=https://abcnews.go.com/International/wireStory/magnitude-76-quake-triggers-tsunami-japans-northern-coast-128208579 |publisher=ABC News |access-date=10 December 2025 |language=en |date=8 December 2025}}</ref>
*[[December 11]] – [[Bulgarian political crisis (2021–2026)]]: The [[Zhelyazkov Government]] resigns following [[2025 Bulgarian budget protests|major protests]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Matoga |first1=Jan |title=Rząd podaje się do dymisji. W Bułgarii zwyciężyła młodość |url=https://www.rmf24.pl/fakty/swiat/news-rzad-podaje-sie-do-dymisji-w-bulgarii-zwyciezyla-mlodosc,nId,8049763 |publisher=RMF 24 |access-date=16 December 2025 |language=pl |date=11 December 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Białczyk |first1=Piotr |title=Polityczne trzęsienie ziemi w Bułgarii. Premier rezygnuje |url=https://wydarzenia.interia.pl/zagranica/news-polityczne-trzesienie-ziemi-w-bulgarii-premier-rezygnuje,nId,22476604 |publisher=Interia |access-date=16 December 2025 |language=pl |date=11 December 2025}}</ref>
* [[December 13]]
** Belarus releases 123 political prisoners including opposition leaders [[Maria Kalesnikava]], [[Maxim Znak]], [[Viktar Babaryka]], Nobel laureate [[Ales Bialiatski]], and journalists [[Pavel Sevyarynets]] and [[Marina Zolotova]] in exchange for the lifting of sanctions on the Belarusian potash industry by the United States.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-12-13 |title=Belarus Frees Opposition Leader, Nobel Laureate in Deal With U.S. |url=https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2025/12/13/belarus-frees-opposition-leader-nobel-laureate-in-deal-with-us-a91435 |access-date=2025-12-13 |website=The Moscow Times |language=en-US}}</ref>
** The [[Junior Eurovision Song Contest 2025]] is held in [[Tbilisi]], [[Georgia (country)|Georgia]]. [[France|French]] contestant [[Lou Deleuze]] wins with the song "[[Ce monde]]".<ref>{{cite web |title=France wins the Junior Eurovision Song Contest 2025 |date=December 13, 2025 |url=https://eurovisionworld.com/esc/france-wins-the-junior-eurovision-song-contest-2025 |access-date=2025-12-13 |publisher=Eurovision World |language=en}}</ref>
* [[December 14]] 
**[[2025 Chilean general election]]: [[José Antonio Kast]] is elected [[President of Chile]]. Right-wing coalitions gain control of the [[Chamber of Deputies of Chile|Chamber of Deputies]] and tie in the [[Senate of Chile|Senate]].<ref>{{Cite news|date=2025-12-15|last1=Villegas|first1=Alexander|last2=Cambero|first2=Fabian|title=Chile elects Kast as president in sharp rightward shift|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/chile-votes-presidential-race-expected-lurch-country-right-2025-12-14/|access-date=2025-12-15|work=Reuters|language=en}}</ref>
**At least 16 people are killed and 43 injured in a [[2025 Bondi Beach shooting|mass shooting]], classified as a [[Terrorism in Australia|terrorist attack]],<ref>{{cite news | title=Bondi beach shooting live updates: two people in custody as PM urges public to follow police guidance amid 'shocking and distressing' scenes | work=[[The Guardian]] | date=14 December 2025 | url=https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2025/dec/14/nsw-police-responding-to-reports-of-shooting-at-sydneys-bondi-beach-follow-latest | access-date=15 December 2025}}</ref> by two gunmen at [[Bondi Beach]] in [[Sydney]] during a celebration for the start of the Jewish festival of [[Hanukkah]].<ref>{{Cite web |title='I have no husband': Victims named after 16 killed in Bondi shooting |url=https://www.nzherald.co.nz/world/i-have-no-husband-victims-named-after-16-killed-in-bondi-shooting/CCJST6CVLNDVHFPK2YJT2A4DVM/ |access-date=2025-12-14 |website=The New Zealand Herald |language=en-NZ}}</ref>
* [[December 19]] – [[European Union|EU]] leaders approve a €90bn ($105bn) loan for [[Ukraine]] for the next two years, which Kyiv will repay only once Russia pays reparations.<ref>{{Cite web |date=19 December 2025 |title=EU agrees €90bn loan for Ukraine as Putin says Kyiv 'refusing to end this conflict'|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/ce8np3pnljdt|access-date=19 December 2025 |website=BBC News|language=en-GB}}</ref>
* [[December 20]] – German engineer [[Michaela Benthaus]] becomes the first [[wheelchair]] user to travel into [[Outer space|space]], aboard the [[Blue Origin NS-37]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=20 December 2025 |title=Engineer becomes first wheelchair user to go to space |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c5y9z0g7lleo|access-date=20 December 2025 |website=BBC News|language=en-GB}}</ref>
* [[December 21]] – [[January 18]] – The [[2025 Africa Cup of Nations]] is held in [[Morocco]], and [[2025 Africa Cup of Nations final|is won]] by [[Senegal national football team|Senegal]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Afcon 2025: Senegal 1-0 Morocco (AET) - Late penalty award sparks chaos |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/cgk8rydnnzkt |access-date=2026-01-18 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref>
* [[December 23]] – [[Harmony Jets Flight 185]], a [[Dassault Falcon 50]], crashes near [[Ankara]], [[Turkey]], killing all eight people on board, including [[Libyan Army]] chief of staff [[Mohammed al-Haddad]].<ref>{{Cite web|date=2025-12-24|title=What we know about the Malta-based private jet that crashed in Turkey|url=https://timesofmalta.com/article/malta-harmony-jet-flight-hmj185-turkey-crash-fault.1121635|access-date=2025-12-31|website=The Times|location=Malta}}</ref>
* [[December 25]] – The [[United States]], in cooperation with the [[Nigeria]]n government, initiates a [[2025 United States strikes in Nigeria|series of airstrikes]] targeting [[Islamic State]]-affiliated militants operating in the country's [[Sokoto State]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=2025-12-25 |title=U.S. strikes ISIS in Nigeria after Trump warnings on Christian killings |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2025/12/25/trump-bombing-nigeria-isis/ |access-date=2025-12-26 |newspaper=The Washington Post |language=en-US |issn=0190-8286}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-12-25 |title=US launches strikes against Islamic State in Nigeria |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj69j8l918do |access-date=2025-12-26 |website=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref> US President Donald Trump states that rising [[Religious violence in Nigeria|extremist violence against Christians]] is a primary reason for the strikes.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Weissert |first=Will |date=2025-12-25 |title=U.S. launches strike against Islamic State forces in Nigeria, Trump says |url=https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-launches-strike-against-islamic-state-forces-in-nigeria-trump-says |access-date=2025-12-26 |website=PBS News |language=en-us}}</ref>
*[[December 26]] – [[Israel]] becomes the first country to recognize [[Somaliland]].<ref>{{cite web|date=26 December 2025|title=Israel becomes first country to formally recognise Somaliland as independent state|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israel-recognises-somaliland-somalias-breakway-region-independent-state-2025-12-26/|website=[[Reuters]]|access-date=26 December 2025 }}</ref>
* [[December 28]] 
** [[2025 Central African general election]]: Incumbent president [[Faustin-Archange Touadéra]] wins reelection for a third term.<ref>{{cite web|last=Muia|first=Wycliffe|title=Central African Republic president wins third term by landslide|date=January 6, 2026 |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c0q40xg3j0jo|access-date=2026-01-06|publisher=BBC|language=en}}</ref>
** [[2025 Guinean presidential election]]: Interim president and [[2021 Guinean coup d'état|2021 coup d'état]] leader [[Mamady Doumbouya]] wins the presidency in a landslide.<ref>{{cite web|title=Guinea coup leader Doumbouya wins presidential election, results show|work=Reuters |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/guinea-coup-leader-doumbouya-wins-presidential-election-provisional-results-show-2025-12-30/|access-date=2025-12-31|language=en}}</ref>
** [[December 2025 Kosovan parliamentary election]]: Incumbent Prime Minister [[Albin Kurti]]'s party [[Vetëvendosje]] wins a fourth consecutive victory, getting 49% of the vote.<ref>{{Cite web|date=2025-12-28|title=Kosovo's leading party wins vote but government formation still unclear|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/12/28/kosovo-votes-in-snap-election-to-end-a-year-of-political-deadlock|access-date=2025-12-31|publisher=[[Al Jazeera]]}}</ref>
** [[2025-2026 Iranian protests|2025 Iranian protests]]: Major protests emerge in [[Iran]] following an intense inflation spike that saw a severe depreciation in the [[Iranian rial]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Protests, strikes after Iran's economic situation rapidly deteriorates|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/12/29/protests-strikes-after-irans-economic-situation-rapidly-deteriorates|access-date=2025-12-29|publisher=Al Jazeera|language=en}}</ref> These protests are accompanied with demands for an end to the [[Government of Iran|Islamic republic]].

