== Nobel Prizes ==
[[File:Nobel medal.png|right|120px|Nobel medal]]
* [[Nobel Prize in Chemistry|Chemistry]] – [[Susumu Kitagawa]], [[Richard Robson (chemist)|Richard Robson]] and [[Omar M. Yaghi]], for the development of metal-organic frameworks.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 8, 2025 |title=Nobel Prize in Chemistry 2025 |url=https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/chemistry/2025/summary/ |access-date=October 8, 2025 |website=[[The Nobel Prize]]}}</ref>
* [[Nobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences|Economics]] – [[Joel Mokyr]], for having identified the prerequisites for sustained growth through technological progress, and [[Peter Howitt (economist)|Peter Howitt]] and [[Philippe Aghion]], for the theory of sustained growth through creative destruction.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 13, 2025 |title=The Sveriges Riksbank Prize in Economic Sciences in Memory of Alfred Nobel 2025 |url=https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/economic-sciences/2025/summary/ |access-date=October 13, 2025 |website=[[The Nobel Prize]]}}</ref>
* [[Nobel Prize in Literature|Literature]] – [[László Krasznahorkai]], for his compelling and visionary oeuvre that, in the midst of apocalyptic terror, reaffirms the power of art.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 9, 2025 |title=Nobel Prize in Literature 2025 |url=https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/literature/2025/summary/ |access-date=October 9, 2025 |website=[[The Nobel Prize]]}}</ref>
* [[Nobel Peace Prize|Peace]] – [[María Corina Machado]], for her tireless work promoting democratic rights for the people of Venezuela and for her struggle to achieve a just and peaceful transition from dictatorship to democracy.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 10, 2025 |title=Nobel Peace Prize 2025 |url=https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/peace/2025/summary/ |access-date=October 10, 2025 |website=[[The Nobel Prize]]}}</ref>
* [[Nobel Prize in Physics|Physics]] – [[John Clarke (physicist)|John Clarke]], [[Michel Devoret|Michel H. Devoret]] and [[John M. Martinis]], for the discovery of macroscopic quantum mechanical tunnelling and energy quantisation in an electric circuit.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 7, 2025 |title=Nobel Prize in Physics 2025 |url=https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/physics/2025/summary/ |access-date=October 7, 2025 |website=[[The Nobel Prize]]}}</ref>
* [[Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine|Physiology or Medicine]] – [[Mary E. Brunkow]], [[Fred Ramsdell]] and [[Shimon Sakaguchi]], for their discoveries concerning peripheral immune tolerance.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 6, 2025 |title=Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine 2025 |url=https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2025/summary/ |access-date=October 6, 2025 |website=[[The Nobel Prize]]}}</ref>

